A decisive failure has already appeared in the paper’s first nonformal step: U-HIT chooses a point in \(C\cap S^\circ\cap S^{\circ\circ}\), although the nonproperness curve \(C\) may be entirely excluded by \(S^{\circ\circ}\). Its preceding fiber-length lemma also identifies a fiber’s structure sheaf with the base change of \(f_*\mathcal O_X\), which is false for proper maps with positive-dimensional fibers. I’m continuing through the degeneration and wedge arguments to determine whether there are additional independent fatal errors and to reconstruct every dependency.
