Corollary 11.2. The finite étale morphism

                                       σ : Y0 → A2

is an isomorphism.

Proof. Since σ is finite étale, the previous theorem implies that it is a disjoint union of
copies of A2 . Because Y0 is irreducible, only one component can occur. Hence σ is an
isomorphism.                                                                             ■

