A.1. Associated graded ring of a DVR
Let (R, m) = (R, (t)) be a discrete valuation ring with residue field κ = R/(t) and valuation
v normalized by v(t) = 1.

Lemma .5. The associated graded ring
                                                   M
                                       grv (R) =         mn /mn+1
                                                   n≥0

is canonically isomorphic to the polynomial ring

                                                  κ[T ],

where T corresponds to the image of t in m/m2 .

Proof. Since R is a DVR, every element x ∈ R can be written uniquely as x = tn u with
u ∈ R× . Thus mn = (tn ) and

                                  mn /mn+1 ∼
                                           = tn R/tn+1 R ∼
                                                         = κ.

The multiplication structure is determined by

                     (tn mod tn+1 ) · (tm mod tm+1 ) = tn+m mod tn+m+1 .

This identifies grv (R) with the polynomial ring κ[T ].                                    ■

Remark .6. Since κ[T ] is a polynomial ring over a field, it is an integral domain. In
particular, T is not a zero-divisor.

